# Downloaded and converted data — regenerable, potentially large
irw_output/
output_noncore/
downloads/

# Item text generated alongside a batch's response tables (SKILL.md Step 3.5),
# staged for upload to the irw_text Redivis dataset. Same lifecycle as
# irw_output/: regenerable from the data/*.py script, and cleared once the
# upload is confirmed. ONLY *__items.csv belongs in here -- itemtext/upload.py
# walks a directory recursively and treats every .csv it finds as a table.
# The durable record is itemtext_provenance.csv, which is tracked.
itemtext_output/

# Ephemeral batch run state
irw_batch_checkpoint.jsonl
*.log

# Optional local reference file for manual dedup checks (library(irw); write.csv(irw_metadata(), ...)).
# Not read by any script — irw_discover_updated.py fetches exclusions live from
# Google Sheets instead — but harmless to ignore if someone generates it by hand.
irw_metadata.csv

# ── Per-run pipeline output: runs/ ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Every disposable per-run artifact -- candidate lists, triage/retriage
# outputs, sanity-check files -- is written to runs/ (see in_runs_dir() in
# irw_discover_updated.py, which every script routes its --out through).
# The whole directory is ignored: these are regenerable from
# search_terms_log.csv + the scripts, and BATCH_LOG.md is the durable
# record of what each run decided. Ignoring it also stops the scheduled
# cloud routines from committing a fresh candidates/triage CSV every week
# (the pile-up that prompted the runs/ move, 2026-08-18).
#
# NOT in runs/, and deliberately tracked -- these are standing, cumulative
# records, not per-run temp files: search_terms_log.csv, plos_seen_dois.csv,
# pmc_seen_dois.csv, repo_triage_seen_keys.csv, license_blocked_candidates.csv,
# plos_deferred_candidates.csv, itemtext_provenance.csv, and human_review/*.csv.
runs/

# Legacy top-level names, kept so an old checkout or a hand-run script that
# still writes to cwd doesn't get committed. New runs land in runs/ instead.
irw_discovered*.csv
candidates*.csv
irw_triage_summary*.csv
irw_triage*.csv
irw_retriage*.csv
triage_test*.csv

# Scratch / test run outputs
test_*.csv

# irw_discover_pmc.py triage output — regenerable, same lifecycle as the
# candidates*.csv / irw_triage*.csv patterns above.
pmc_triage*.csv
pmc_test*.csv

# journal_scout/ raw API response cache — regenerable (skip-if-exists reruns
# rebuild it), and grows large (~40MB) since it holds one JSON file per
# journal/year/query-variant and per sampled article. The CSVs it feeds
# (journals_resolved.csv, step2_yearly_counts.csv, step3_supp_manifest.csv,
# step4_license.csv, journal_yield.csv, journal_yield_summary.md) are the
# actual deliverables and stay tracked.
journal_scout/cache/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
